  "body": "Was stacked on #405 (#318), which has merged; this branch has `origin/main` merged in and targets `main`.\r\n\r\n## What changed\r\n\r\n- **A later setup's verdict never sees less material than the carried body.** When an op's setup is entered with a carried body (#317 / #318's chain), `operation::carried_stock::judged` checks the setup's declared stock against the incoming body. The first check is cheap: the origin stock box carried uncut through the turns. If that fails, the real carried grid is cut and its bounds are clamped to the uncut block. If the declared stock is a box that already holds the body, nothing changes. Otherwise the job's `stock_facets` / `stock_aabb` become the box enclosing both. Every stock-reading law reads that box: the rapid-in-stock column and footprint rings, the stock top, the entry/plunge solid, reach, top-stock, and the tilted slab. The prior acquittal still clears dives into material earlier setups really cut. The post blocks on the same cached WARN records, so post and generation agree.\r\n- **A mismatch is named, and refused wherever a feed move cuts into it** (review round 2). If a feed move reaches carried material outside the declared stock, the path carries `operation::CARRIED_OUTSIDE_DECLARED`, which names both setups, the overhang and the move, and the post gate (`operation::carried_problems`) refuses by name. The reach test reads the carried grid's columns under each feed chord's footprint box. An overhang that no feed move reaches is only noted (`CARRIED_OUTSIDE_NOTED`).\r\n- **Declared material beyond the carried block is present** (#405 review a). Where the declared stock reaches past the uncut carried block in XY, neither verify's prior nor the rest mask is read, and the raw stock judges. Before this, the prior acquitted a dive there because its disc still caught the grid's low edge cells. The fix is pinned, and the test fails without it.\r\n- **A refused carry refuses every op of the setup**, posed ones included. Before, only ops that read the prior were refused. A posed op in a carried setup now carries the rest-chain digest in its stamp (`rest::carried_digest`). No other stamp moves.\r\n- `rest::across`: `carried_stock_block`, `carried_stock_body`, `carried_digest`. `carried_grid` can stop at the body the consumer setup is entered with.\r\n\r\n## Not done here (refused or owed, see `docs/decisions/319-carried-verify.md`)\r\n\r\n- Non-rest kinds still use the declared stock as their machining region (Face, 2D pocket/adaptive, contour). Carried material outside it is judged but not machined, and the note says so. A declared stock larger than the carried body still cuts air there. Pocket3D and Multi-Axis Rough already bound their cut by #318's mask. Bounding every kind's region is #320's stock-source question.\r\n- Lateral rapids are still acquitted only as today: vertical dives only (#96).\r\n- #408 (#320, the per-setup stock source) is not merged yet. This code keys on `carry::entry` through #318's chain, so whichever PR lands second makes the chain honour the source.\r\n\r\n## Pinning tests\r\n\r\n`crates/app/tests/carried_verify.rs` (new, 5 tests):\r\n- `a_dive_clear_of_the_declared_block_into_carried_material_is_refused`: Setup2's declared top is 5 and the carried body stands to 9. The contour's dive is convicted, the note names Setup1/Setup2, and `post_setup` is blocked on that rapid move.\r\n- `a_dive_into_material_setup1_removed_is_allowed`\r\n- `a_flipped_carry_judges_the_dive_against_the_flipped_body` (#405 review c)\r\n- `declared_stock_beyond_the_carried_block_is_judged_present` (#405 review a; it fails with the prior read)\r\n- `a_turn_off_the_quarter_with_only_a_non_rest_op_after_it_is_refused_by_name` (#405 review b). With a 30-degree turn, the non-rest op's generation is refused with `CARRY_TURN_REFUSAL` naming both setups, and the program sim and the gate never judge it. With every op of the setup now refused at generation, `simulate_document` cannot reach the carry itself: it refuses earlier, on the stale op.\r\n\r\n## Gate (on the tree merged with current main)\r\n\r\nDebug, own target dir, camcraft-app: carried_verify (5), rest_across_setups (5), setup_carry (5), vertical_rapid_stock (10), posting (17), golden_cl (23, goldens unchanged), stock_sim_document (9), setups (11), operations (117 + 6 ignored), drill_prior (12), drill_prior_kinds (4), top_stock (4), remachining (6), suppressed_rest (2), setup_relative (8), setup_align (9), stock_stamp (4), lib (95). All green. clippy `-D warnings` on camcraft-app, all targets: clean. The sim crate is not touched.\r\n\r\nChangelog: In a later setup that holds the body carried from earlier setups, rapids, entries and links are judged against that body even where it stands outside the setup's declared stock. A feed move into carried stock outside the declared stock refuses the post by name, any other mismatch is noted, and a carry the lattice cannot hold refuses every operation of that setup.\r\n\r\nFixes #319\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\n",
